From 30ff60e13cd46a1ee97e916ecddf333b8e8b9cea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jose Castillo <jcastillo@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 09:38:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [upload] Add --preauth option to pre-authorize a system

Add a --preauth option to `sos upload` that runs the device
authorization flow and prsists the OIDC refresh token locally,
without uploading a file. This removes the interactive,
browser-based authentication step from the upload itself, allowing
a system to be authorized ahead of time for later unattended or
scripted uploads.

The FILE argument is now optional so that `sos upload --preauth`
can be run on its own; a missing FILE without --preauth still
reports an error.

Related: RHEL-29345

Signed-off-by: Jose Castillo <jcastillo@redhat.com>
---
 man/en/sos-upload.1            |  8 ++++++++
 sos/upload/__init__.py         | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 sos/upload/targets/__init__.py | 12 ++++++++++++
 sos/upload/targets/redhat.py   | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 sos/upload/targets/ubuntu.py   |  8 ++++++++
 5 files changed, 84 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/man/en/sos-upload.1 b/man/en/sos-upload.1
index 53494667..b33a5e8c 100644
--- a/man/en/sos-upload.1
+++ b/man/en/sos-upload.1
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@ sos_upload \- Upload files like previously generated sos reports or logs to a po
           [--upload-s3-access-key key]\fR
           [--upload-s3-secret-key key]\fR
           [--upload-s3-object-prefix prefix]\fR
+          [--preauth]\fR
 
 .PP
 .SH DESCRIPTION
@@ -136,6 +137,13 @@ Secret key for the S3 bucket
 .B \--upload-s3-object-prefix PREFIX
 Prefix for the S3 object/key
 
+.TP
+.B \-\-preauth
+Pre-authorize this system by running the authentication flow and storing
+the resulting token locally (see \fBTOKEN STORAGE\fR), without uploading a
+file. Useful to prepare a system for later, unattended uploads. Only
+supported for upload targets that use token-based authentication.
+
 .SH TOKEN STORAGE
 When using web-based authentication for uploads, \fBsos\fR stores the
 refresh token locally in the file \fI~/.sos-oidc-token.json\fR so that
